-- title:
--   Pinning in one unramified over-layer gives the local fundamental class
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and work inside a fixed algebraic closure `PadicAlgCl q` of $\mathbb{Q}_q$. Let $L$ be an intermediate field, finite over $\mathbb{Q}_q$, let $G$ be a finite group acting faithfully on $L$ by semiring automorphisms which fix every element of the image of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ (hypothesis `hG`), equipped with a multiplicative-distributive action on $L^\times$ compatible with the action on $L$ (hypothesis `hcompat`), and let $K$ be an intermediate field, finite over $\mathbb{Q}_q$, which is a base for $(L,G)$ in the sense that $K \le L$ and an element of $L$ lies in $K$ exactly when it is fixed by all of $G$. Suppose given one unramified over-layer datum: an intermediate field $M$ finite over $\mathbb{Q}_q$ with $L \le M$, a finite group $H$ acting faithfully on $M$ with a compatible action on $M^\times$, normal subgroups $N_L, N_n \trianglelefteq H$, an isomorphism $e : G \simeq H/N_L$, an element $\varphi \in H$ and a unit $\pi \in M^\times$, together with $d$ asserting: $H$ fixes $\mathbb{Q}_q$ pointwise; the unit and field actions agree; $K$ is the $H$-fixed subfield of $M$ and $L$ the $N_L$-fixed subfield; the $G$-action on $L$ and the $H$-action on $M$ correspond under $e$; $\#(H/N_n) = \#G$; $H/N_n$ is generated by the image of $\varphi$; on $N_n$-invariant elements of norm at most $1$ the element $\varphi$ acts as the residual Frobenius, $\|\varphi \cdot x - x^{\#\kappa}\| < 1$ with $\kappa$ the residue field of `Rw q K`; and $\pi$ is $H$-invariant, lies in $K$, has norm $< 1$, and has maximal norm among $N_n$-invariant elements of norm $< 1$. Let $u \in H^2(G, L^\times)$, the second cohomology of the representation `Rep.ofMulDistribMulAction G (↥L)ˣ` over $\mathbb{Z}$. Assume the pin equation for this single datum: for every morphism $\iota$ from the restriction of $L^\times$ along $H \to H/N_L \xrightarrow{e^{-1}} G$ to $M^\times$ which on units induces the inclusion $L \subseteq M$ inside `PadicAlgCl q`, and for all proofs that the image $\bar\varphi$ of $\varphi$ in $H/N_n$ has finite order and that `carryFun` applied to $\bar\varphi$ and to the $N_n$-invariant element `Additive.ofMul π` (the function sending $(g_1,g_2)$ to that element when the cyclic logarithms of $g_1$ and $g_2$ to base $\bar\varphi$ sum to at least $\mathrm{ord}(\bar\varphi)$, and to $0$ otherwise) is a $2$-cocycle, the image of $u$ under the degree-$2$ map induced by $H \to G$ and $\iota$ equals the inflation from $H/N_n$ of the class of that carry cocycle. The conclusion is `IsLocalFundamentalClass q L G K u`: the same pin equation holds for every unramified over-layer datum over $(L,G,K)$ and every such $\iota$.
--
--   This is the statement that the local fundamental class of the layer $(L/K, G)$ may be pinned down using a single unramified over-layer: the normalisation by the carry cocycle of a lifted Frobenius and a uniformiser of $K$ is independent of the chosen over-layer. It is the existence half of the characterisation of the local fundamental class, and is used in the uniqueness-and-existence statement [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.existsUnique_isLocalFundamentalClass`](thm.html#ExtCitation.LocalLevel.existsUnique_isLocalFundamentalClass), in its compatibility with field inclusions [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.isLocalFundamentalClass_map_subtype`](thm.html#ExtCitation.LocalLevel.isLocalFundamentalClass_map_subtype), and in the local computation [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.inflate_sub_unitsInflate2_carryFun_mem_levelCoboundaries2`](thm.html#NumberField.PlaceDecomp.inflate_sub_unitsInflate2_carryFun_mem_levelCoboundaries2).
